1. 📦 Import
import java.util.*;
📌 Overall meaning:

Imports all utility classes like ArrayList, Scanner, List etc.

🧩 Terms:
import → includes external packages
java.util → package containing utility classes
* → imports ALL classes inside package
⭐ Alternatives:
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;

👉 (better practice: import only what you need)

🎤 Viva line:

“This imports utility classes like ArrayList and List from java.util package.”

2. 🧱 Product Class
class Product
📌 Overall meaning:

Defines blueprint for product details.

🧩 Terms:
class → blueprint
Product → user-defined class name
⭐ Alternatives:

No direct alternative (OOP structure required)

3. 🔒 Variables (Encapsulation)
private int id;
private String name;
private double price;
private int quantity;
📌 Overall meaning:

Stores product details securely.

🧩 Terms:
private → access only inside class
int → whole numbers
String → text
double → decimal values
⭐ Alternatives:
public (not recommended → breaks encapsulation)
protected (for inheritance cases)
🎤 Viva line:

“We use private access modifier to achieve encapsulation and protect data.”

4. 🏗️ Default Constructor
public Product()
📌 Overall meaning:

Creates product with default values.

🧩 Terms:
public → accessible outside class
Product() → constructor (same name as class)
⭐ Alternatives:
No-arg constructor manually setting values elsewhere
🎤 Viva line:

“Default constructor initializes object with default values.”

5. 🏗️ Partial Constructor
